@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hvac-nouns`

-- hvac-fees-regs.l4 -- the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or
-- Air-Conditioning Systems (Fees) Regulations 5785-2025, in THREE vintages:
--
--   Draft       the SimpLEX screenshot (Figure 4 of Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov & Gelbard 2025).
--               The screenshot shows reg 1, reg 2(a)-(e) in full, and the HEADING of reg 3.
--               It does NOT show the body of reg 3, reg 4, reg 5 or the signature block.
--               What it does not show, this module does not know, and says so with a named
--               REFUSE.  Reg 4 is known only through the SimpLEX test panel's own gloss.
--   As made     Kovetz HaTakanot 11951, 9 July 2025, p. 2116.
--   As amended  Kovetz HaTakanot 12383, 4 May 2026 (p. 2062); consolidated text: Hebrew
--               Wikisource rev 3011135 (unofficial; used here as an aid, not an authority).
--
-- Three vintages are three answers, never merged.  Every lookup takes the vintage as an
-- input.  Where a vintage is silent on a service the answer is NOTHING ("this vintage
-- prescribes no fee for that service"), never a number borrowed from another vintage.
-- Amounts are in new Israeli shekels (שקלים חדשים).
--
-- The Law's power to prescribe fees is ss 59-60 (outside the pinned scope: cited, not
-- encoded).  The preamble of the regulations, as made:
@@Q fees 10@@

-- ============================================================================
§ `Regulation 1: Definitions`
-- ============================================================================

-- AS MADE, reg 1 defines ONE exam, the practical exam:
@@Q made 20~\.1\sהגדרה 21 22@@
--
-- AS AMENDED (12383 s 1) adds the theory exam after it:
@@Q amend 21 22 23@@
--
-- DRAFT (screenshot, as read from a low-resolution crop; the wording may contain
-- misreadings): defines both "בחינה עיונית" and "בחינה מעשית".  The draft words the
-- practical exam as an assessment of the knowledge and practical skills "of the pupil"
-- ("של התלמיד"), where the regulations as made say "of a learner in a vocational
-- training course".  The draft's Chapter A is headed "מטרה והגדרות" (purpose and
-- definitions); the regulations as made head it "הגדרות" (definitions) only.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 1
GIVEN v IS A Vintage
GIVETH A LIST OF `Exam kind`
`the exams that regulation 1 defines under` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN Draft        THEN LIST `Theory exam`, `Practical exam`
    WHEN `As made`    THEN LIST `Practical exam`
    WHEN `As amended` THEN LIST `Theory exam`, `Practical exam`

-- ============================================================================
§ `Regulation 2: Fees`
-- ============================================================================

-- THE DRAFT.  Reg 2(א)-(ה) as the screenshot shows it (low-resolution crop, read by eye):
--   (א) בעד בחינה עיונית, תשלום אגרה בסכום של 273 שקלים חדשים.
--   (ב) בעד בחינה מעשית, תשלום אגרה בסכום של 194 שקלים חדשים.
--   (ג) הוגש ערעור על הבחינה העיונית או המעשית, יתווסף לתשלום בעד האגרה כאמור בסעיף קטן (א),
--       סכום של 40 שקלים חדשים, בעד כל ערעור.
--   (ד) בעד בקשה לקבלת רישיון או לחידושו לפי סעיף 5 לחוק, תשלום אגרה בסכום של 284 שקלים חדשים.
--   (ה) בעד בקשה לקבלת רישיון זמני למומחה זר או לחידושו לפי סעיף 8 לחוק, תשלום אגרה בסכום של 398 שקלים חדשים.
-- Four things the draft does that the regulations as made do not:
--   * it prices a THEORY exam (273);
--   * it speaks of an "ערעור" (appeal), where the regulations as made say "השגה" (objection);
--   * its 2(ג) adds the 40 "to the payment ... as stated in subsection (א)", i.e. the
--     THEORY exam fee, even for an appeal on the practical exam (fork F-F4);
--   * it charges for the APPLICATION (בקשה) for a licence, where the regulations as made
--     charge for RECEIVING it (קבלת רישיון) (fork F-F2).
-- Its 2(ה) cites "סעיף 8 לחוק" for the temporary licence of a foreign expert; in the
-- Law as enacted and in the bill at third reading that licence is section 9.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 (draft, SimpLEX Figure 4) reg 2(a)-(e)
GIVEN s IS A `Fee service`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the draft's regulation 2 prescribes, for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `a theory exam`                                                          THEN JUST 273   -- draft 2(א)
    WHEN `a practical exam`                                                       THEN JUST 194   -- draft 2(ב)
    WHEN `an objection to a theory exam score`                                    THEN JUST 40    -- draft 2(ג)
    WHEN `an objection to a practical exam score`                                 THEN JUST 40    -- draft 2(ג)
    WHEN `an application for a licence or its renewal`                            THEN JUST 284   -- draft 2(ד)
    WHEN `receiving a licence or its renewal`                                     THEN NOTHING    -- draft 2(ד) charges for the application
    WHEN `a request for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its renewal` THEN JUST 398   -- draft 2(ה)
    WHEN `a refresher training under section 17`                                  THEN NOTHING    -- none of draft 2(א)-(ה)

-- AS MADE, reg 2 (Kovetz HaTakanot 11951 p. 2116).  Every amount printed here is the base
-- amount of 2025: regulation 3 updates them each 1 January (see below).
@@Q made 24~\.2\sאגרות@@
--
@@Q made 26 27@@
--
@@Q made 28 29@@
--
@@Q made 30 31@@
-- The regulations as made have no theory exam: it is neither defined nor priced, so the
-- three theory rows are NOTHING.  Their 2(ב) speaks of "the exam" ("הבחינה"), and the only
-- exam reg 1 defines is the practical one, so the objection fee attaches to the practical
-- exam alone (fork F-F5).  2(ג) is a fee for RECEIVING a licence, not for applying.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 (as made, Kovetz HaTakanot 11951) reg 2(a)-(d)
GIVEN s IS A `Fee service`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 2 as made prescribes, for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `a theory exam`                                                          THEN NOTHING    -- no theory exam in this vintage
    WHEN `a practical exam`                                                       THEN JUST 194   -- 2(א)
    WHEN `an objection to a theory exam score`                                    THEN NOTHING    -- no theory exam in this vintage
    WHEN `an objection to a practical exam score`                                 THEN JUST 40    -- 2(ב)
    WHEN `an application for a licence or its renewal`                            THEN NOTHING    -- 2(ג) is for receiving, not applying
    WHEN `receiving a licence or its renewal`                                     THEN JUST 284   -- 2(ג)
    WHEN `a request for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its renewal` THEN JUST 398   -- 2(ד)
    WHEN `a refresher training under section 17`                                  THEN NOTHING    -- no fee prescribed (s 59 permits one)

-- AS AMENDED (12383 ss 1-2).  The amendment inserts 2(א1) and changes 2(ב) in two places:
-- it inserts "העיונית" after "ציון הבחינה", and it replaces the cross-reference "(א)" by
-- "(א1)".  The amendment leaves 2(א), (ג) and (ד) as made.  Consolidated text, Wikisource
-- rev 3011135 (unofficial), which also annotates the amounts "מתואם לשנת 2025" for
-- 194, 40, 284 and 398, and "מתואם לשנת 2026" for 158:
@@Q fees 24@@
@@Q fees 25@@
@@Q fees 26@@
@@Q fees 27@@
@@Q fees 28@@
-- THE HEADLINE FINDING.  After the amendment, 2(ב) reaches only an objection on the score
-- of the THEORY exam ("הבחינה העיונית") and is added to 2(א1).  No provision in this
-- vintage prescribes a fee for an objection on the score of the PRACTICAL exam.  The 40
-- shekels as made is NOT carried over: the answer for that service is NOTHING.  Whether
-- that is a policy choice or a drafting slip the sources do not say (fork F-F6).
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 (as amended, Kovetz HaTakanot 12383) reg 2(a), (a1), (b), (c), (d)
GIVEN s IS A `Fee service`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 2 as amended prescribes, for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `a theory exam`                                                          THEN JUST 158   -- 2(א1)
    WHEN `a practical exam`                                                       THEN JUST 194   -- 2(א)
    WHEN `an objection to a theory exam score`                                    THEN JUST 40    -- 2(ב) as amended
    WHEN `an objection to a practical exam score`                                 THEN NOTHING    -- 2(ב) as amended reaches the theory exam only
    WHEN `an application for a licence or its renewal`                            THEN NOTHING    -- 2(ג) is for receiving, not applying
    WHEN `receiving a licence or its renewal`                                     THEN JUST 284   -- 2(ג)
    WHEN `a request for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its renewal` THEN JUST 398   -- 2(ד)
    WHEN `a refresher training under section 17`                                  THEN NOTHING    -- no fee prescribed (s 59 permits one)

-- The reading of 2(ב) taken throughout: the objection fee is ON TOP of the exam fee that
-- the examinee has already paid ("נוסף על התשלום בעד האגרה"): an objection costs 40, not
-- the exam fee over again plus 40 (fork F-F3).  The figure is per objection ("בעד כל השגה").
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 2
GIVEN v IS A Vintage
      s IS A `Fee service`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the fee prescribed under` v `for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN Draft        THEN `the draft's regulation 2 prescribes, for` s
    WHEN `As made`    THEN `regulation 2 as made prescribes, for` s
    WHEN `As amended` THEN `regulation 2 as amended prescribes, for` s

-- The objection fee for n objections: 40 each (all vintages that prescribe one).
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 2(b), draft 2(ג): "בעד כל השגה" / "בעד כל ערעור"
GIVEN v IS A Vintage
      n IS A NUMBER
      s IS A `Fee service`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the total fee prescribed under` v `for` n `of` s MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fee prescribed under` v `for` s
    WHEN NOTHING   THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST fee  THEN JUST (fee TIMES n)

-- ============================================================================
§ `Regulation 3: Updating the fees`
-- ============================================================================

-- AS MADE and AS AMENDED (the amendment does not touch reg 3):
@@Q fees 31@@
@@Q fees 32@@
@@Q fees 33@@
@@Q fees 34@@
@@Q fees 35@@
-- DRAFT: the screenshot shows only the heading "3. עדכוני אגרות", and the SimpLEX test panel
-- for "תרחישי בדיקה לעדכוני אגרות ומדד" (relevant: Law s 59, regulations 3(א)-(ב)) is cut
-- off before its first scenario.  The draft's reg 3 is unknown.

-- An exact half is not covered by "to the nearest whole new shekel", so it refuses.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 3(a): "ויעוגל לשקל החדש השלם הקרוב"
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest whole new shekel` x MEANS
    BRANCH IF (x MINUS FLOOR x) LESS THAN 0.5    THEN FLOOR x
           IF (x MINUS FLOOR x) GREATER THAN 0.5 THEN (FLOOR x) PLUS 1
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "regulation 3(a) says 'rounded to the nearest whole new shekel' and does not say which way an exact half goes"

-- The first update day after commencement is the first 1 January after the day the
-- regulations commenced ("יום העדכון הראשון שלאחר יום תחילתן של תקנות אלה").
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 3(a), "יום העדכון הראשון"
GIVETH A DATE
`the first update day after the regulations commenced` MEANS
    YMD ((DATE_YEAR `the day the principal regulations commenced`) PLUS 1) 1 1

-- The November index of a given year, from the series the caller supplies.  No index value
-- is invented here: a year the series does not hold refuses.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 3(a), "המדד שפורסם בחודש נובמבר"
GIVEN year         IS A NUMBER
      `the series` IS AN `Index series`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the index published in the November of` year `in` `the series` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the year of the November` EQUALS year) (`the series`'s `published in the Novembers`)
    WHEN EMPTY             THEN REFUSE "the supplied index series holds no reading for that November"
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN r's `the index published then`

-- "המדד החדש": the index published in the November before the update day.
-- "המדד היסודי": the index published in the November before the PREVIOUS update day, and,
-- for the first update day after commencement, the index published in the month before
-- commencement.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 3(a), "המדד היסודי"
GIVEN year         IS A NUMBER
      `the series` IS AN `Index series`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base index for the update on 1 January of` year `in` `the series` MEANS
    IF   year EQUALS DATE_YEAR `the first update day after the regulations commenced`
    THEN `the series`'s `published in the month before the regulations commenced`
    ELSE `the index published in the November of` (year MINUS 2) `in` `the series`

-- One update step.  The step is applied to the amount in force just before the update day:
-- the base index is only ever one year back, so the amounts compound, each year rounded
-- (fork F-R3).  The text is the same in the regulations as made and as amended.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 3(a)
GIVEN amount        IS A NUMBER
      year          IS A NUMBER
      `the series`  IS AN `Index series`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount` amount `after the update of 1 January` year `by` `the series` MEANS
    `rounded to the nearest whole new shekel`
        ((amount TIMES `the index published in the November of` (year MINUS 1) `in` `the series`)
            DIVIDED BY `the base index for the update on 1 January of` year `in` `the series`)

-- Regulation 3(b): "יפרסם" -- the Director General SHALL publish, by notice in Reshumot, the
-- text of regulation 2 as it has changed.  A duty with no time stated, so no WITHIN.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 3(b)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Fees Regulations` `Act under the Fees Regulations`
`regulation 3(b): the Director General shall publish regulation 2 as updated` MEANS
    PARTY `the Director General of the Ministry of Labour`
    MUST  `publish in Reshumot the text of regulation 2 as changed by the update`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- ============================================================================
§ `Regulation 4: Payment of a fee as a condition of a licence or of an exam`
-- ============================================================================

-- AS MADE and AS AMENDED (unchanged by 12383):
@@Q fees 38@@
-- DRAFT: not shown.  The SimpLEX panel glosses it as "תקנה 4: אוסרת רישום ללא תשלום"
-- (regulation 4 prohibits registration without payment) and gives, for "registration for
-- an exam without payment", the outcome "השעיית שירות".  Both are the tool's words, not
-- the regulation's.  This module encodes reg 4 for the draft from that gloss, for exams
-- only, and refuses everywhere the gloss says nothing (fork F-D1).

-- Regulation 4 reaches a licence, a required exam and the filing of an objection on an
-- exam, in each case "שנקבעה בעדו/בעדן אגרה" (for which a fee was set).  A refresher training
-- is none of the three.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 4
GIVEN s IS A `Fee service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 4 covers a service of the kind` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `a refresher training under section 17` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 4: "הבחינות הנדרשות" (the required exams)
GIVEN s IS A `Fee service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the service is an exam` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `a theory exam`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a practical exam` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Is full payment a condition of the service?  Only where a fee WAS set for it.  A vintage
-- that sets no fee for the service imposes no payment condition on it (NOTHING above makes
-- this FALSE rather than a refusal).  A temporary licence is "a licence for which a fee was
-- set" (fork F-F7).
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 4
GIVEN s IS A `Fee service`
      v IS A Vintage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` s `under` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN Draft THEN
        IF   `the service is an exam` s
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE REFUSE "the draft's regulation 4 is not shown in the screenshot; the SimpLEX panel glosses it only for registration for an exam"
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the fee prescribed under` v `for` s
        WHEN NOTHING   THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST fee  THEN `regulation 4 covers a service of the kind` s

-- The service may be given only on full payment where reg 4 so provides.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 4: "אלא אם כן ... שילם את האגרה במלואה"
GIVEN s    IS A `Fee service`
      v    IS A Vintage
      paid IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 4 permits` s `under` v `given payment in full is` paid MEANS
    IF   `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` s `under` v
    THEN paid
    ELSE TRUE

-- ============================================================================
§ `Regulation 5: Commencement`
-- ============================================================================

-- AS MADE (and the principal regulations as amended):
@@Q fees 41@@
-- The regulations as made were published in Kovetz HaTakanot 11951 on 9 July 2025:
@@Q made 4@@
-- Seven days from publication, with the day of publication not counted, is 16 July 2025.
-- The unofficial consolidation annotates reg 5 "(התקנות פורסמו ביום 9.7.2025, ותחילתן ביום
-- 16.7.2025)" and the Law's s 63(a)(1) annotation says the same.  Counting the day of
-- publication as the first of the seven would give 15 July (fork F-R5).
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 5
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the principal regulations were published` MEANS YMD 2025 7 9

@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 5
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the principal regulations commenced` MEANS
    `the day the principal regulations were published` PLUS 7

-- The amending regulations were published in Kovetz HaTakanot 12383 on 4 May 2026:
@@Q amend 4@@
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 (amendment), Kovetz HaTakanot 12383, date of issue
GIVETH A DATE
`the day Kovetz HaTakanot 12383 was published` MEANS YMD 2026 5 4

-- The amending regulations (12383) contain NO commencement provision: ss 1 and 2 amend regs
-- 1 and 2 and the text ends with the Minister's signature, 11 Iyar 5786 (28 April 2026).
-- When the amendment came into force is therefore not in the sources.  Publication is a
-- common default, but a default is not in the text, and it is not taken.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 (amendment), Kovetz HaTakanot 12383 -- no commencement provision
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the 5786 amendment commenced` MEANS
    REFUSE "Kovetz HaTakanot 12383 states no commencement date, so the sources do not say when the 5786 amendment came into force"

-- The draft: regulation 5 is not shown.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 (draft, SimpLEX Figure 4) reg 5
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the draft's regulation 5 would have commenced` MEANS
    REFUSE "the draft's regulation 5 is not shown in the SimpLEX screenshot"

-- The commencement of the principal regulations, in each vintage.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 5
GIVEN v IS A Vintage
GIVETH A DATE
`the principal regulations commenced, under` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN Draft        THEN `the day the draft's regulation 5 would have commenced`
    WHEN `As made`    THEN `the day the principal regulations commenced`
    WHEN `As amended` THEN `the day the principal regulations commenced`

-- The vintage in force on a day.  The draft is never selected: it was never in force.
-- Before 16 July 2025 no fee regulations were in force at all.  From 4 May 2026 the sources
-- do not say whether the amendment was in force (above), so the answer refuses.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 5; Kovetz HaTakanot 12383
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE Vintage
`the vintage in force on` d MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN `the day the principal regulations commenced`        THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN `the day Kovetz HaTakanot 12383 was published`        THEN JUST `As made`
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "from the day Kovetz HaTakanot 12383 was published the sources do not say whether the 5786 amendment was in force"

-- If the caller supplies the amendment's commencement, the answer needs no refusal.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 5; Kovetz HaTakanot 12383
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the day the amendment commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE Vintage
`the vintage in force on` d `if the amendment commenced on` `the day the amendment commenced` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN `the day the principal regulations commenced` THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN `the day the amendment commenced`             THEN JUST `As made`
           OTHERWISE JUST `As amended`

-- The fee payable on a day.  The printed amounts are the 2025 base amounts; regulation 3
-- updates them each 1 January, and the sources contain neither an index value nor a notice
-- under reg 3(b).  So the printed amount answers only for a day before the first update day.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 3(a) and reg 5
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      s IS A `Fee service`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the fee payable on` d `for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vintage in force on` d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no fee regulations were in force`
    WHEN JUST v  THEN
        IF   d LESS THAN `the first update day after the regulations commenced`
        THEN `the fee prescribed under` v `for` s
        ELSE `the printed fee has been updated by regulation 3`

@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 5
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no fee regulations were in force` MEANS
    REFUSE "no fee regulations under ss 59-60 were in force before the principal regulations commenced"

@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 3(a)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the printed fee has been updated by regulation 3` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 3(a) updates the printed amounts on each 1 January and the sources contain no index values and no notice under regulation 3(b), so the amount payable from 1 January 2026 is not in them"

-- ============================================================================
§ `The SimpLEX test panel: the scenarios run against a vintage`
-- ============================================================================

-- The panel "תרחישי בדיקה לבחינות מקצועיות" (test scenarios for professional exams),
-- "סעיפים רלוונטיים: חוק – סעיף 9 | תקנות – 2(א)-(ה)", has four rows (numbered 5 to 8 in the
-- screenshot) and a worked example beneath it.  What the rows say they do, and what they do
-- not say, is in NOTES.md.  The code below is the encoder's reading of how each vintage
-- answers a scenario, from regulations 2 and 4.

@ref SimpLEX Figure 4: what the scenario is about
GIVEN sc IS A `SimpLEX scenario`
GIVETH A `Fee service`
`the fee service of` sc MEANS
    CONSIDER sc's `the request`
    WHEN `registration for an exam` THEN
        CONSIDER sc's `the exam`
        WHEN `Theory exam`    THEN `a theory exam`
        WHEN `Practical exam` THEN `a practical exam`
    WHEN `an appeal against an exam score` THEN
        CONSIDER sc's `the exam`
        WHEN `Theory exam`    THEN `an objection to a theory exam score`
        WHEN `Practical exam` THEN `an objection to a practical exam score`

-- What the panel prints when the fee has been paid in full and nothing bars the request:
-- the panel's words, for the kind of request.  "Registration approved" says more than
-- regulation 2 does -- it removes the payment bar and approves nothing else (fork F-T3).
@ref SimpLEX Figure 4, test table rows 5 to 7
GIVEN sc IS A `SimpLEX scenario`
GIVETH A `SimpLEX outcome`
`the panel's word for success in` sc MEANS
    CONSIDER sc's `the request`
    WHEN `registration for an exam`        THEN `registration approved`
    WHEN `an appeal against an exam score` THEN `the appeal is examined`

-- Not paid, and regulation 4 makes payment a condition: the panel's word is "השעיית שירות"
-- (service suspension) for registration without payment, row 8.  The same facts are given
-- a second outcome by the worked example, "registration rejected, payment must be
-- completed"; one function cannot return both (fork F-D2).
@ref SimpLEX Figure 4, test table row 8; Fees Regulations 5785-2025 reg 4
GIVEN v  IS A Vintage
      sc IS A `SimpLEX scenario`
GIVETH A MAYBE `SimpLEX outcome`
`the outcome of non-payment under` v `for` sc MEANS
    IF   `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` (`the fee service of` sc) `under` v
    THEN JUST `service suspension`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The outcome of a SimpLEX scenario under a vintage.  NOTHING: the vintage prescribes no fee
-- for what the scenario is about and so says nothing about the scenario.
@ref Fees Regulations 5785-2025 regs 2 and 4
GIVEN v  IS A Vintage
      sc IS A `SimpLEX scenario`
GIVETH A MAYBE `SimpLEX outcome`
`the SimpLEX outcome under` v `for` sc MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fee prescribed under` v `for` (`the fee service of` sc)
    WHEN NOTHING   THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST fee  THEN
        IF   sc's `the fee was paid in full`
        THEN JUST (`the panel's word for success in` sc)
        ELSE `the outcome of non-payment under` v `for` sc
